Single: Returns one element of a list. In other words, we use ".Single()" when we know the list has ONLY one element. If no element is found or multiple elements pass the condition, it'll throw an exception. 
 So in these cases, we should use ".SingleOrDefault()".

SingleOrDefault: Returns one element of a sequence and if no element is found then it will return the default value of that type

First: Returns the first element of a list. We use ".First()" when we are sure that there is at least one element (I mean maybe there are more than one element in a list and we want the first one). 
Sometimes we determine a condition in parentheses and ".First()" returns the first element that passes the condition.
If the list is empty or no element passes the condition, it throws an exception. So in these cases, we should use ".FirstOrDefault()".

FirstOrDefault: Returns the first element of a sequence and if no element is found then it will return the default value of that type.
